{{also|Duodenum}}
==English==
[[Image:Tractus intestinalis duodenum.svg|thumb|A schematic of the [[gastrointestinal tract]], with the duodenum shown in orange-pink.]]

===Etymology===
From {{ML.}} (from the phrase {{term||duodēnum digitōrum|space of twelve digits}}, in reference to its length), from {{term|duodeni|duodēnī|twelve each|lang=la}} + {{term|digitorum|digitōrum|lang=la}}, genitive plural of {{term|digitus||finger, toe, [[digit]]|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/djuːə(ʊ)ˈdiːnəm/}}
* {{audio|en-us-duodenum.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|duodena|pl2=duodenums}}

# The first part of the [[small intestine]], starting at the lower end of the [[stomach]] and extending to the [[jejunum]].

====Derived terms====
* [[duodenal]]
* [[duodenitis]]

====Synonyms====
* [[dodecadactylum]], [[maw-gut]] {{i|both obsolete}}

